1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,800
Narrator: Scenario 30. Network and access.

2
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:16,488
B: The vendor API responds from my laptop, but production calls time out after ten seconds. The application code and requested endpoint are the same.

3
00:00:17,088 --> 00:00:29,232
A: The connection path differs between your laptop and production. Production uses an outbound proxy, so we need to compare DNS, proxy routing, and destination access.

4
00:00:29,832 --> 00:00:40,128
C: Please provide the failed request time and the observed public source IP through our support ticket. We will check the corresponding access records.

5
00:00:40,728 --> 00:00:52,344
A: I will share the approved egress details there. First, I am checking whether the timeout occurs during proxy connection, TLS negotiation, or the API response.

6
00:00:52,944 --> 00:01:03,408
B: The trace reaches the proxy, but it shows no completed TLS session with the vendor. Should we increase the application timeout to thirty seconds?

7
00:01:04,008 --> 00:01:14,088
A: A longer timeout would not resolve a blocked connection and could tie up more workers. Let us identify the failed connection stage before changing it.

8
00:01:14,688 --> 00:01:24,984
C: I see connection attempts from an address outside your registered range. Did the production egress address change during your recent proxy maintenance?

9
00:01:25,584 --> 00:01:36,336
A: The maintenance added a second approved proxy gateway, but its public address is absent from the vendor request. I will verify both active gateways.

10
00:01:36,936 --> 00:01:46,728
B: Can we force production through the original gateway until the update is approved? We need to consider whether that would reduce capacity or redundancy.

11
00:01:47,328 --> 00:01:56,976
A: We will assess that option with the network owner. The preferred fix is to update the vendor allowlist through the existing approval process.

12
00:01:57,576 --> 00:02:09,120
C: Once approved, I can add the exact new address and coordinate a test at 18:00 UTC. Please send requests through each gateway separately.

13
00:02:09,720 --> 00:02:21,264
A: I will coordinate those tests and verify successful business responses, not just open connections. We will attach results and add vendor checks to the maintenance checklist.
